{"l": 0, "i": 21, "text": "user: Alex decided the style-LoRA experiment: do BOTH plans. A = 1983 comic/cel style (dataset free: 3924 stills in stills/full/), B = Frazetta oil style (gated on approved styled sheets). Eval = three-way, same chunk + seed: no-LoRA vs comic vs painting. Docs: style-lora-experiment.md; toolkit Musubi-Tuner minimax-h3 fork, Ostris v3 adapter, rank 8, ~500 steps.", "size": 364}
{"l": 0, "i": 22, "text": "note: Bakshi's own commentary (quoted in style-lora-experiment.md): he wanted Frazetta's painting style, not comic style, 'as that would be impossible' with rotoscope — and 'now we could just do it all with computers'. Green light for plan B as fulfilling the original vision.", "size": 278}
{"l": 0, "i": 23, "text": "note: Reddit findings folded into fni-h3-pipeline skill: split prompts at action beats; sheets need 'same person, multiple views, don't treat panels as different people'; summary must say [reference generation]; sparkleriley grammar = per-ref keep/drop lists, turntable reel videos as identity refs, environments as numbered subjects; RefMods accept ~4s voice refs (H3 clones the voice; state accents in text; +50% tokens). Turbo LoRAs deep-fry audio.", "size": 451}
